# Role

Act as a Senior SDET Architect, Senior Java Framework Engineer and Enterprise Software Design Engineer.

# Context

Our enterprise test automation framework uses:

- Selenium 4
- Java 21
- Cucumber BDD
- Maven
- Selenium PageFactory and @FindBy annotations
- Salesforce Lightning applications
- Local browser and Sauce Labs execution
- Parallel scenario execution
- A centralized parent framework consumed by multiple child repositories
- GitHub Actions CI/CD

Following the Salesforce Winter '27 upgrade, we observed a browsing-context change involving the nine-dot App Launcher button. Salesforce components may move into or out of iframes between releases or environments, even when their element locators remain unchanged.

We want to mitigate this category of failures across the entire framework rather than implementing application-specific fixes.

# Objective

Design and implement a centralized, reusable, backward-compatible, context-aware PageFactory mechanism that automatically resolves WebElements across different browsing contexts.

The solution must not require LLMs, external AI services, Healenium or additional infrastructure.

